    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0265" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/267a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Yokohama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scidmore</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following for Stevens [from Willard]:</p>
                <p>Your cable 4th.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d328-f1"/> Fifty thousand dollars cabled
                    January 3 for Emerson. Have answered all your cables. Advise immediately if
                    matter is now fixed. Do not be discouraged. You will not be deserted. Am hoping
                    you will still find opportunity to do great good.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
